 "audit": "Not able to deliver ten novel findings: only about four associations are not already known, and those are the least certain. Several cautions. (1) Extreme hypermutators exist (up to ~9000 mutated genes vs median 6); cases above 300 genes were excluded. (2) Embryonal rhabdomyosarcoma has a high median burden (24), so its low-count hits in long passenger genes (FCGBP, DNAH11, ADGRL3, etc.) were dropped as likely burden artifacts, not signal. (3) Diagnosis labels are heterogeneous and overlapping (NOS, 'Glioma, malignant', 'missing'/'Unknown'), so comparison groups mix tumor types and can create apparent associations (Simpson-type confounding); the Pilocytic astrocytoma PIK3R1 excess (30/168) is odd and may be a cohort or labelling artifact or a calling artifact. (4) Many diagnoses have tiny n; small-count hits (n<15) are fragile. (5) Possible duplicate or related patients, no per-case sequencing/panel metadata, so unequal gene coverage cannot be ruled out. (6) Many tests (234 candidate pairs); BH FDR applied but the comparison background is not independent of the labeled categories.",
